  "inscription": "Stone: (405 Squadron RCAF badge)/ Just before Midnight/ on 1st September 1942/ HALIFAX II BB216 (LQ-D)/ of 405 Squadron RCAF/ from Topcliffe/ crashed near this spot/ following a disastrous engine fire/ This memorial is placed here to/ commemorate the crew members who died/ (names) Plinth: IN GRATEFUL REMEMBRANCE Planter plagues: (405 Squadron RCAF badge)/ THEY WILL/ NEVER GROW/ OLD Vase: RAOB",
